            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "The Sage"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Finally, a way to use up the leftover cream cheese! I had half a block (4 oz.) that needed to be used. Scrounging in the pantry yielded a bag of about 30 chocolate chips. To this, imagining a cheesecake, I added 1/8 teaspoon of raspberry extract and 2 tablespoons of sugar. You can hardly go wrong with cream cheese, chocolate, and sugar.",
            "datePublished": "2018-04-29T00:35:34.047Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Karen Rogers"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very tasty and easy. I added 1/2 t. Vanilla to the cream cheese mixture. Used low fat cream cheese. Used thin layer of graham crackers crumbs on bottom. Layered with mini chocolate chips and chocolate sundae syrup. Topped with a few mini chocolate chips, more syrup, half strawberry and blackberry. Good, fast small dessert recipe. Thanks!",
            "datePublished": "2017-03-06T12:47:35.263Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "alerose"
            },
            "reviewBody": "Used little shot cups and did only the chips at the bottom, one layer of cream cheese and topped with mini m&amp;m's. Good one serving dessert for a picnic today.",
            "datePublished": "2015-07-04T06:50:51.437Z"
          },
          {
            "@type": "Review",
            "reviewRating": {
              "@type": "Rating",
              "ratingValue": "4"
            },
            "author": {
              "@type": "Person",
              "name": "Baker's Dozen"
            },
            "reviewBody": "This was very good and easy to make. I did modify it by adding 2 teaspoons of vanilla extract, reducing the sugar to 1/2 cup and omitting the chips on the bottom. I also used less chocolate chips and just folded them into the cream cheese mixture instead of layering, and drizzled chocolate syrup and whipped cream on top when served. Next time, I'll make it the same way but use mini chocolate chips.",
            "datePublished": "2015-04-05T21:30:54.947Z"
